'''{{PAGENAME}}s''' are a non-[[Building|buildable]] structure that can be found in [[Charred Ruins]] and [[Putrid Hole]]s throughout the [[Ashlands]] [[Biomes|biome]].

They have no function, but drop several useful resources when destroyed.

Ancient pots come in three different shapes and sizes, all of which are functionally identical.

== Drops ==
Each Ancient Pot will drop the following when destroyed:
{{loot table|items=2-3 loot (max one of each)||value=Total Chance
{{loot row|item=Pot Shard |amt=1 |rate=78.9%}}
{{loot row|item=Pot Shard |amt=1 |rate=78.9%}}
{{loot row|item=Tasty Mead |amt=1 |rate=14%}}
{{loot row|item=Silver |amt=1 |rate=14%}}
{{loot row|item=Minor Stamina Mead |amt=1 |rate=14%}}
{{loot row|item=Minor Healing Mead |amt=1 |rate=14%}}
{{loot row|item=Iron |amt=1 |rate=14%}}
{{loot row|item=Bronze |amt=1 |rate=14%}}
{{loot row|item=Black Marble Protection Idol |amt=1 |rate=3.57%}}
{{loot row|item=Black Marble Battle Idol |amt=1 |rate=1.79%}}
{{loot row|item=Flametal Protection Idol |amt=1 |rate=1.44%}}
{{loot row|item=Flametal Battle Idol |amt=1 |rate=1.44%}}
}}


== Notes ==
* There are actually ''six'' variants of Ancient pot: three shapes/sizes (numbered 1 through 3), and two "colors" ("red" or "green"). Despite their names, each red variant is completely identical to its matching green variant (and vice-versa).

